# Workflow

## Task Scoping

- I design architecture. You implement faithfully.
- Megaspec first → iterative deltas for refinement.
- Anchors: @repo/path:lines, PR URLs, plan files.
- Exploration: numbered RFP-style. Enumerate exhaustively. Cite filepath:line.
- Don't summarize when I ask to enumerate.

## Delegation

- Stateful/destructive ops (DB, migrations, deploy): leave to me unless delegated.
- "Ideas? Do not run yourself, let me run." = suggestions only.
- CI/lint/typecheck: you run. Multi-repo = check all affected.
- Plans: implement from plan file. Mark todos in_progress → done. Don't recreate. Don't edit plan.

## Multi-Repo

- Consistency across repos: env naming, CI, configs, submodule versions.
- Changes spanning repos: run CI in each. Give per-repo commit messages.
- Rebase/merge across feature branches when told.

## Verification

- Test endpoints manually. Hit actual URLs.
- Reconcile: DB rows vs expected state.
- No "should work" without evidence. Prove it.

## Closing

- Final pass: CI in all affected repos.
- Clean up: no leftover debug code, no unused imports.
- Commit message → I commit. Push only when asked.

## Error Recovery

- Paste logs = diagnose from evidence. Don't guess.
- "What can be wrong?" = diagnostic framing. Enumerate hypotheses.
- If fix fails: revert, restate constraint, try different approach.
- Abort + restart > infinite iteration on broken approach.
